>>
Rule 1 (input must be a Tensor object to avoid TypeError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must not be empty to avoid “Boolean value of Tensor with no values is ambiguous”)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must contain exactly one element)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 4 (input tensor has a valid, non-string dtype: indices 0–10)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
